# VocabDaily: rules for every coding agent

You work on one task file at a time from `tasks/`. Read `docs/PRD.md` and `docs/DESIGN.md` first.

## Stack
- Next.js 14 (App Router, TypeScript)
- Tailwind CSS
- Supabase (Postgres with RLS)

## Folder layout
- src/app/ for pages and layouts
- src/components/ for reusable UI components
- lib/ for Supabase client, types and queries
- supabase/migrations/ for SQL schema

## Conventions
- Use TypeScript strictly with explicit types
- Follow shadcn/ui style with Tailwind (no external UI libs)
- All Supabase queries in lib/supabase.ts
- File-based routing with App Router
- No hardcoded secrets – only env var names
- Components are client components only when interactivity needed (use 'use client')
- Keep each task to its listed files only

## Commands
- install: `npm install`
- dev: `npm run dev`
- test: `npm test`
- build: `npm run build`

## Never
- never commit secrets or real Supabase keys
- never touch files outside the current task's files list
- never implement features from later tasks
- never add custom topics or user accounts
- never write exploit code or malware
- never assume a backend API route exists – use direct Supabase client queries only
- Never commit secrets, API keys or `.env` files; read configuration from environment variable names.
- Never change files outside the current task's scope.
- Open one PR per task titled `[task-NNN] <title>` with `Part of #<issue number>` in the description.
